    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f6bee3d3-1e5a-5c4a-9346-975f5bb72a83",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $y=\\sqrt{-8x+5}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=-8x+5.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-8.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot -8 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{-8x+5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
